      <floats-group id="article-23646.s17">
        <fig id="article-23646.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Dorsal Forearm Anatomy. Intersection syndrome affects the first and second compartments of the dorsal wrist extensors. These extensors are part of a collective of 6 dorsal compartments that are variably responsible for wrist and digital extension. CFCF, <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1120_Muscles_that_Move_the_Forearm_Antebrach._Sup._Ext._Sin.png">Public Domain</ext-link>, via Wikimedia Commons</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Dorsal__forearm__anatomy" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
